# The title screen. The shortest scenario there is: it needs no assets past
# the ones the boot path loads, and it fails first when the boot path breaks.
name: title
summary: Boot through the logos to the title screen, press START, then New Game.
frames: 2000
pad: 1600:start,1640:a
env: SOA_RENDER=1
env: SOA_SNAP=50

shows: the whole boot path, which is most of the runtime: the DOL loaded and
shows:   entered, OS init, the DVD reads that stage the title, the DSP booted,
shows:   the first EFB copies, and the title backdrop's two cloud quads (the
shows:   rasteriser's row-span bug lived in those, FINDINGS "The title's black
shows:   wedges").
shows: that the SI model delivers a scripted press: START at frame 1600 is
shows:   taken by the title, A at 1640 chooses New Game.

evidence: build/boot_title.log, which prints "[si] 2 scripted controller
evidence:   events" and then frame 1600 buttons 1000 (START), 1610 buttons 0000,
evidence:   frame 1640 buttons 0100 (A), 1650 buttons 0000 -- a press at 1600 and
evidence:   another at 1640, each released after the default ten-frame hold.
evidence: the same log writes build/frames/NNNN.png every 50 frames, which is
evidence:   where SOA_SNAP=50 comes from.
